From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 13:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi_em: release removed client-stat cache entries

hash_map_remove() transfers ownership of the removed AP-metrics client-stat
entry to the caller.  The disassociation path discarded that returned pointer,
leaking one entry for every client departure.

The fresh upstream OneWifi revision already releases the encoded EasyMesh
event buffers covered by the earlier version of this patch (cd27b70c,
RDKBWIFI-498).  Retain only this independent, still-missing cache fix so the
layer neither duplicates nor double-frees the upstream ownership changes.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 source/apps/em/wifi_em.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c b/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
index 01cf2e5..0b5481a 100644
--- a/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
+++ b/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
@@ -1678,6 +1678,7 @@ static int em_handle_disassoc_device(wifi_app_t *app, void *arg)
     }
     wifi_util_dbg_print(WIFI_EM, "%s:%d: Sta Mac %s disassociated\n", __func__,
         __LINE__, sta_mac_str);
+    free(stats);
 
     to_mac_str((unsigned char *)assoc_data->dev_stats.cli_MACAddress, client_mac);
     sta_client_info_t *t_sta_data = (sta_client_info_t *)hash_map_remove(
-- 
2.43.0
